Z||000010||Fformula88||11-30-2001||10:06 AM||||The Fiero Store, although some on here see them as the great Satan (not the hockley player!), is actually a great resource for the Fiero community... as is Rodney, Archie, and many others.<P>The Fiero Store has been and will continue to try and keep parts in production, and/or get parts that are discontinued back into production.  <P>As Fiero's get older and certain parts get to become more rare, it will be nice to have a few places that offer good products and reliable service to turn to.<P>Long live them all!<P>------------------<BR>John  <BR>AOLIM: Fformula88<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/formulasig.JPG">           <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">    <P>1988 Fiero Formula<BR>1985 Fiero SE 2M6||||reg||1
Z||000011||Raydar||11-30-2001||10:53 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fformula88:<BR><B>The Fiero Store, although some on here see them as the great Satan... </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Do you really think people still see them in that way?<P>They made an exceedingly bad business move.<BR>They were called on it. Loudly.<BR>They apologized. Profusely.<BR>They made amends (didn't they?) to the injured party.<P>Good enough for me (and, I suspect, most others), although the other party will always be my first choice. Just because. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT><p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 11-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||Rodney||11-30-2001||11:13 AM||||I guess it is to be expected but they have taken me off their mailing list now. <P><BR>Some of their new products I'm sure are just items soon to be offered in the aftermarket anyway. I had talked to Year One and Soft Seal on door gaskets etc a few years ago. I'm guessing someone like that will be making them and also selling them. A couple items may be original though. I'm curious to see if there exhaust hangers just happen to be just like mine.  : )<P>||||reg||1
Z||000013||88CoupeV6||11-30-2001||11:21 AM||||I have had great luck with the Fiero store. The Stuff is always at my doorstep the next day and the people on the phone are super nice. I have always had great quality from them too. Same with the many products I have got from "Rodney the man"  The list goes on with Mr Mikes, Fiero dave, and Doug at the Fiero warehouse. I think I must buy too much stuff.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88coupeV6.jpg">        <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>    <A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com/nefa.htm" TARGET=_blank>Join New England Fiero Association</A><p>[This message has been edited by 88CoupeV6 (edited 11-30-2001).]||||reg||7
Z||000014||88CoupeV6||11-30-2001||11:29 AM||||I forgot to mention how special Bob parker at kick hill farms is. He opens his home to our fiero club for meetings and events and even gives pizza and soda. I always leave feeling like I robbed the guy leaving with a car load of stuff and he only charges like $50. I got a rear fascia for $50 and he let me use his tools to put it on there. He even said if I don't like it when it comes back from the paint shop he will give me my money back. His barn has 3 floors of fiero parts. It is like a candy store for Fiero owners.||||reg||7
